From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] lab(#53 w1b): cap the detail repaint inset by the paint's
 slack per side

Wave 1 challenger (6f2ef5d2) dropped the inset only on image-edge
sides. Lab probe: when sharpPlan's budget/cap fallback paints coverage
== crop (2.5x on the Blue 201MP pyramid), interior sides have no slack
either, so the same crop still "escaped" and repainted ~9x/s at rest.

slackInsets() caps each side's early-repaint inset by the slack the
painted coverage had beyond the painted crop on that side; the
image-edge case is the zero-slack special case. Experimental candidate
for Quackles Lab; not for promotion without phone evidence.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
